Drop the UNO embind JavaScript glue from the WASM build

The generated UNO/JavaScript embind bridge (static/unoembind) projects the
ENTIRE UNO API -- every interface, method, struct, enum and enumerator -- into
JavaScript as Module.uno. This product never uses it. Conversion is driven
through the LibreOfficeKit C entry points (libreofficekit_hook_2 /
lo_initialize, and the init_office / convert_document wrappers in
desktop/source/app/wasm_bridge.cxx). Module.uno is written at startup and never
read, by LibreOffice or by us.

It is not even reachable. init_unoembind_uno() has exactly one caller,
initUno() in desktop/source/app/appinit.cxx, which runs from
Desktop::InitApplicationServiceManager() <- Desktop::Init() <- soffice_main().
LOK is initialised with SAL_LOK_OPTIONS=unipoll (set by wasm_bridge.cxx), and
in unipoll mode lo_initialize() calls InitVCL() and never starts soffice_main();
the only other caller, lo_runLoop(), is never invoked by this product. The
runtime trace confirms it -- "[LO_INIT] eStage=2 bUnipoll=1" followed by
"[LO_INIT] Unipoll mode: calling InitVCL()", with no soffice_main.

MEASURED COST OF CARRYING IT (documents module, this tree):

  soffice.js   the generated init_unoembind_uno() is 587,697 of the 891,012
               bytes of soffice.js, and 59,346 of the 114,475 bytes of
               soffice.js.br -- 51.8% of the compressed JavaScript every
               visitor downloads. Measured by deleting the function and
               re-running the pipeline's own `brotli -q 11`, which reproduces
               the shipped soffice.js.br byte for byte.

  soffice.wasm 3,884,622 bytes of the 67,033,307-byte code section across
               18,549 functions (5.79%), attributed by walking the WebAssembly
               name section of the linked, unstripped soffice.wasm and summing
               function bodies whose names are unoembind*, the_wrappers::*,
               *embindtest*, or emscripten::internal::* instantiated over UNO
               types. bindings_uno.o is 61,076,802 bytes in libunoembind.a; the
               PrimaryBindings.o kept beside it is 54,544.

ONE NON-OBVIOUS CONSEQUENCE, CHECKED: bindings_uno.cxx calls registerUnoType<T>()
for every UNO type, which ODR-uses typeid(T) and so emits the typeinfo for every
UNO exception. desktop/CustomTarget_soffice_bin-emscripten-exports.mk feeds
wasmbridgegen's list of 246 __ZTI... symbols to -sEXPORTED_FUNCTIONS, and for 71
of them bindings_uno.o is the ONLY definition anywhere in workdir (verified by
grepping every .o and .a in the build tree; control: __ZTIN3com3sun4star2io11-
IOExceptionE appears in 140 objects, __ZTIN3com3sun4star13configuration7backend-
39InvalidAuthenticationMechanismExceptionE in exactly one). They are the
exception types no LibreOffice source file mentions at all.

That does NOT break the link: emsdk 3.1.51 (tools/building.py) passes every
EXPORTED_FUNCTIONS entry as --export-if-defined=, never --export=, so wasm-ld
drops the ones with no definition. Only REQUIRED_EXPORTS is a hard --export.

And it does not break exception handling: bridges/source/cpp_uno/gcc3_wasm/
cpp2uno.cxx getRtti() looks the symbol up with jsGetExportedSymbol() and, on
null, synthesizes a __class_type_info / __si_class_type_info at runtime -- the
same fallback the native gcc3 bridge takes when dlsym misses. In practice the
71 affected types cannot be thrown anyway: no code in the tree names them.

WHAT IS KEPT: PrimaryBindings (uno_Type / uno_Any / uno_Sequence and the
getUnoComponentContext helper). It is small, self-contained, and keeping it
means libunoembind.a still exists and is still non-empty -- so the
-Wl,--whole-archive $(call gb_StaticLibrary_get_target,unoembind) reference,
which every per-module add-ucb-sfx-libraries-*.patch rewrites, needs no change.
bindings_uno.{cxx,hxx,js} are still generated by CustomTarget_unoembind (so
sofficeapp's use_custom_headers stays valid); they are simply no longer
compiled or linked. That also removes a 7.9 MB translation unit from the build.

Every site touched is EMSCRIPTEN-only already: static/ is added to the build
only under ifeq (EMSCRIPTEN,$(OS)) in static/Module_static.mk, the
Executable_soffice_bin.mk block is inside ifeq ($(OS),EMSCRIPTEN), and the
appinit.cxx code is inside #if defined EMSCRIPTEN. Native builds are untouched.

Affects: static/StaticLibrary_unoembind.mk
         desktop/Executable_soffice_bin.mk
         desktop/source/app/appinit.cxx
         static/emscripten/uno.js

diff --git a/desktop/source/app/appinit.cxx b/desktop/source/app/appinit.cxx
--- a/desktop/source/app/appinit.cxx
+++ b/desktop/source/app/appinit.cxx
@@ -53,7 +53,10 @@
 #include <emscripten.h>
 #include <emscripten/threading.h>
 #include <emscripten/val.h>
-#include <bindings_uno.hxx>
+// WASM: <bindings_uno.hxx> declared exactly one thing, init_unoembind_uno(),
+// and nothing below calls it any more. The generated UNO embind bindings are
+// no longer compiled into libunoembind.a either -- see
+// static/StaticLibrary_unoembind.mk for the rationale and the numbers.
 #include <config_emscripten.h>
 #endif
 
@@ -140,7 +143,18 @@
 }
 
 void initUno() {
-    init_unoembind_uno();
+    // WASM: init_unoembind_uno() published the ENTIRE UNO API to JavaScript as
+    // Module.uno. This product never drives conversion that way -- it goes
+    // through the LibreOfficeKit C entry points (libreofficekit_hook_2 /
+    // lo_initialize), so Module.uno is written and never read.
+    //
+    // initUno() is in fact unreachable here. It runs from
+    // Desktop::InitApplicationServiceManager(), which runs from Desktop::Init(),
+    // which runs from soffice_main(). LOK is initialised with
+    // SAL_LOK_OPTIONS=unipoll, and in unipoll mode lo_initialize() calls
+    // InitVCL() instead of starting soffice_main(); nothing in this product
+    // calls lo_runLoop(), which is the only other caller. The call is removed
+    // rather than #if'd out because the definition it needs is no longer built.
     std::vector<std::u16string> urls;
 #if __EMSCRIPTEN_PTHREADS__
     emscripten_sync_run_in_main_runtime_thread(EM_FUNC_SIG_VI, getUnoScriptUrls, &urls);
diff --git a/desktop/Executable_soffice_bin.mk b/desktop/Executable_soffice_bin.mk
--- a/desktop/Executable_soffice_bin.mk
+++ b/desktop/Executable_soffice_bin.mk
@@ -95,14 +95,19 @@
 endif
 
 $(call gb_Executable_get_linktarget_target,soffice_bin): \
-    $(gb_CustomTarget_workdir)/static/unoembind/bindings_uno.js \
     $(SRCDIR)/static/emscripten/uno.js \
     $(EMSCRIPTEN_EXTRA_SOFFICE_PRE_JS)
 
 $(eval $(call gb_Executable_add_prejs,soffice_bin,$(SRCDIR)/static/emscripten/script.js))
 
+# WASM: bindings_uno.js is the JavaScript half of the UNO embind bridge -- a
+# single generated init_unoembind_uno() function that names every UNO type,
+# interface, method and enumerator. In the shipped documents module it is
+# 587,697 bytes of the 891,012-byte soffice.js, and 59,346 bytes of the
+# 114,475-byte soffice.js.br: 52% of the compressed JS we make every visitor
+# download. It only ever ran from Module.uno_init$resolve(), which is dead --
+# see static/emscripten/uno.js and desktop/source/app/appinit.cxx.
 $(eval $(call gb_Executable_add_ldflags,soffice_bin, \
-    --post-js $(gb_CustomTarget_workdir)/static/unoembind/bindings_uno.js \
     --post-js $(SRCDIR)/static/emscripten/uno.js \
     $(foreach i,$(EMSCRIPTEN_EXTRA_SOFFICE_PRE_JS),--pre-js $(i)) \
 ))
diff --git a/static/StaticLibrary_unoembind.mk b/static/StaticLibrary_unoembind.mk
--- a/static/StaticLibrary_unoembind.mk
+++ b/static/StaticLibrary_unoembind.mk
@@ -13,9 +13,38 @@
     static/source/unoembindhelpers/PrimaryBindings \
 ))
 
+# WASM: bindings_uno.cxx is embindmaker's projection of the ENTIRE UNO API into
+# embind -- 7.9 MB of generated C++ that compiles to a 61 MB object (vs 54 KB
+# for PrimaryBindings.o next to it). Measured in the linked, unstripped
+# soffice.wasm of the documents module, it accounts for 3,884,622 bytes of the
+# 67,033,307-byte code section across 18,549 functions (5.79%): the
+# init_unoembind_uno() registrar, the the_wrappers::* interface shims, the
+# emscripten::internal::* invokers instantiated for UNO types, and the
+# org::libreoffice::embindtest scaffolding.
+#
+# Its only entry point is init_unoembind_uno(), whose only caller was
+# desktop/source/app/appinit.cxx's initUno(). That function is unreachable in a
+# LibreOfficeKit build: LOK initialises with SAL_LOK_OPTIONS=unipoll, and in
+# unipoll mode lo_initialize() calls InitVCL() and never soffice_main(), so
+# Desktop::Init() -> InitApplicationServiceManager() -> initUno() never runs.
+# This product converts documents through the LOK C entry points, never through
+# the UNO/JS bridge. Nothing else links against symbols defined here:
+# bindings_uno.cxx defines only static register*() helpers plus
+# init_unoembind_uno(); PrimaryBindings.cxx is a provider, not a consumer.
+#
+# PrimaryBindings is deliberately kept: it is small, self-contained, and leaving
+# it means libunoembind.a still exists and is still non-empty, so the
+# -Wl,--whole-archive $(call gb_StaticLibrary_get_target,unoembind) reference in
+# desktop/Executable_soffice_bin.mk (rewritten by every per-module patch) needs
+# no change at all.
+#
+# ifneq below is belt-and-braces: static/ is only built for EMSCRIPTEN
+# (see static/Module_static.mk), so this is EMSCRIPTEN-only by construction.
+ifneq ($(OS),EMSCRIPTEN)
 $(eval $(call gb_StaticLibrary_add_generated_exception_objects,unoembind, \
     CustomTarget/static/unoembind/bindings_uno \
 ))
+endif
 
 $(eval $(call gb_StaticLibrary_use_api,unoembind,\
     offapi \
diff --git a/static/emscripten/uno.js b/static/emscripten/uno.js
--- a/static/emscripten/uno.js
+++ b/static/emscripten/uno.js
@@ -11,7 +11,10 @@
 
 Module.uno_init = new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {
     Module.uno_init$resolve = function() {
-        Module.uno = init_unoembind_uno(Module, Module.unoTagSymbol);
+        // WASM: bindings_uno.js is no longer --post-js'd into soffice.js, so
+        // init_unoembind_uno() does not exist and Module.uno is never built.
+        // See desktop/Executable_soffice_bin.mk. Nothing in this product reads
+        // Module.uno -- conversion goes through the LibreOfficeKit C API.
         resolve();
     };
     Module.uno_init$reject = reject;
